 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Once upon time, in the big woods behind your house, there was small fire pit where people would gather after dark to sing and tell stories. One night, as the moon brightened, someone set small Torch in middle of the pit. Everyone gathered around it and sang songs as the torch burned down. Oh yes, it was. People believed that spirits needed no fire to talk, only silence and darkness. He's probably just curious. You could ask him who he'd like to talk to, and then stop everyone from talking after he does. Sure. Why don't ghosts ever get lost? Because they've always been at the same address.",
